{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony","id":291969,"title":"Conspiracy: The Order of St Anthony","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-25T05:55:57-07:00","id":291969,"title":"Conspiracy: The Order of St Anthony","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:26px\">The Order of St Anthony</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Gravediggers</span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ask any grandmother and you\u2019ll learn the truth: The dead left unburied shall walk again; and the Eastern Bloc has unburied dead in legion. It is a holy duty to restore slumber to the dead, and the Gravediggers work tirelessly. Six foot by six foot their hands turn raw and bloody on the shovels. Their muscles burn, their stomachs rumble and they dig on.<br /> <br /> In 1453 an orthodox bishop named Ivanovich Vasin learned that there was truth in old wives tales when he was attacked by walking corpses. Wounded he walked to Moscow to warn the Patriarch, but Ivanovich never noticed that he died during the journey. When he arrived before Jonah of Moscow the Patriarch saw his ephemeral visitor as a sign from God and quickly agreed to sponsor the Order of St. Anthony.<br /> <br /> Five hundred years is a long time to uphold the vigil, and during those five hundred years the order has suffered greatly. Yet they did not suffer at the hands of monsters, or at least not monsters with fangs and unholy powers. Mankind is more powerful than any vampire or necromancer, and when mankind turned on their protectors the results were swift and brutal.<br /> <br /> In 1921 the Soviet Union began a campaign against the Eastern Orthodox Church. A key objective of this campaign was the elimination of the Church\u2019s military wing; by all accounts the Order put up a damn good fight. They were well trained, disciplined, and Benedictions had a psychological component that went beyond their battlefield effectiveness; but despite these advantages they were outnumbered, outgunned, and ultimately defeated.<br /> <br /> [picture: A last stand is taking place at a small rural church. A barricade of sandbags blocks the doorway and two rural parishioners take cover behind the sandbags shooting towards the perspective. Behind them stands a priest holding up an Icon of St. Martin. Bullets fired towards the defenders miraculously curve away in mid air; but a rocket propelled grenade is in mid flight and on target.]<br /> <br /> The survivors spent three decades in hiding. Three decades moving from safe house to safehouse. Three decades relying on sympathisers to stay alive, any one of whom may be bribed, blackmailed, or a Soviet agent. Even during those dark days many still upheld their duties in secret - they were more concerned of the account they would give to God than the gulags.<br /> <br /> After those three decades things became easier. When the Great Patriotic War began Stalin and the Eastern Orthodox Church signed a truth, and the Church was allowed to rebuild. The terms of this truce strictly forbade the church from running it\u2019s own military, but those terms were ignored. With support from the Church the Order began to secretly rebuild throughout the Soviet Union and even beyond, far from the eyes of anyone searching for them.<br /> <br /> With the fall of the Soviet Union the Gravediggers have emerged from the hiding places, ready to put down all the monsters created from a century of atrocities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Enemy</span><br /> <br /> The Eastern Front, the holocaust, the purges. Modern history has not been kind to Eastern Europe. Pockets of spiritual and necromantic turmoil cover the continent, and the Gravediggers are holding the shovel.<br /> <br /> The Order of St. Anthony might have named themselves for the patron saint of gravediggers, but they do not see themselves as hunters of the undead. They see themselves as protectors of humanity and hunters of all Satan\u2019s legion. Their specialisation is an act of necessity, not ideology.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are the most common dead being the Gravediggers encounter, and the Order considers them to be morally equivalent to humans. If a Ghost is incapable of speech they will give it an exorcism and the last rites. If the Ghost is lucid they\u2019ll invite it for a final confession. The Order knows that many Ghosts depart on their own accord if their final requests are fulfilled and considers doing so to be a charitable act but they aren\u2019t above convincing or forcing a ghost into exorcism if it\u2019s unfinished business is immoral or impractical.<br /> <br /> The Gravediggers also work to bury the remains of the past in a somewhat literal fashion. They use Benedictions to purify the corruption left at the site of battlefields or atrocities. There are places where exorcists have been purifying taint for decades and isolated locations where the Order has trapped zombie hordes inside a ring of Benedictions powered by bunker-shrines until such time as the monsters can be put six feet under.<br /> <br /> Ghostwalkers are especially hated. The Orders consider Ghostwalkers to be possessed by demons attracted to the necromantic corruption. The Bound\u2019s tendency to create death cults, to control the dead, and to adorn themselves with parodies of the sacred and occult are all evidence for a sinful nature. The Ghostwalker\u2019s apparent immunity to exorcism only serves as further proof of their willing partnership with Satan.<br /> <br /> If the Order of St. Anthony thinks Vampires aren\u2019t as bad as Ghostwalkers, the difference is slight. The leeches are kind of monster only fit for a deathbed repentance, emphasis on the \u201cdeathbed\u201d. Witches and necromancers? They got their power from bargain with Satan.<br /> <br /> All Conspiracies occasionally but heads with other Conspiracies but the Order of St. Anthony is deeply entangled with the occult politics of Eastern Europe. In some countries it is the dominant Conspiracy but in other countries the Order must avoid the watchful eye of ex-Soviet Conspiracies who now serve the new governments or their own interests. The Eastern Orthodox Church is using it\u2019s political issue to promote and protect it\u2019s Hunters, but progress is slow. And let no one forget the long and turbulent history between the Eastern Orthodox and the Catholic Churches.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hunters</span><br /> <br /> You were a krokodil addict, you\u2019ve stopped using but it\u2019s too late. You\u2019re dying, your body is rotting away, hell you\u2019ve seen zombies better looking than you. But you\u2019re not dead yet, you\u2019re holding yourself together with willpower and Benedictions. If you\u2019re going to die, you\u2019re going to die doing the Lord\u2019s work.<br /> <br /> You're an old man. You should be retired by now, but the Conspiracy needs your unique skills. In the 1930s you were a young hunter for the Serbian branch of the Gravediggers, one of the few significant branches to remain untouched by the Soviets. Refugees, the few lucky ones who made it, they came from all over the Soviet Union carrying what sacred artefacts and tomes they could. You fought alongside them, you learned from them, and you became one of the best masters of Benedictions in the Order, and now that the Gravediggers are moving back into their old haunts you're the one recovering what they lost. You interrogate ghosts, dig through burned out monasteries, and even organise occasional raids on old soviet facilities. It's a dangerous and important job.<br /> <br /> You were a farmer. To you the Reds and the Whites were far less important than getting food onto your family\u2019s table. You\u2019d chant any slogan people asked if it meant the government would leave you alone. Then they came for the Church and that was a step too far. A monk came begging to your door and you offered to hide him. But old habits die hard, when he heard vampires were hunting nearby he started going back at night. One night he didn\u2019t come back, and you knew nothing until you saw him in a newspaper decades later. You wrote him a letter and started putting supplies in that old safe room just encase anyone needs it again.<br /> <br /> You were a priest during the times of the Soviet Union. One day you got a tap on the shoulder. He told you about the risen dead, the consequences of atrocities, he left you texts on Benedictions and told you to train. When the Soviet Union fell you got a call, and you're ready to do your holy duty.<br /> <br /> Your family was smuggled out of Russia by sympathisers, but there wasn't much opportunity for Eastern Orthodox Priests in America. You never went hungry, but you never had much either. Growing up poor you fell in with a rough crowd, the Bratva. You always feared the confrontation with your father, but to your surprise he came to offer a deal, not condemnation. He taught you things that kept you safe in the Underworld, and in return you sent weapons to his old friends. Now the Order's star is rising, and they've made a simple offer. Switch sides, become one of our men inside the Bratva. Fight for the good guys and work off that debt against your immortal soul. Benedictions are real, why not hell? You took the offer, and you took a lot of your loyal men with you.<br /> <br /> You were never a part of of the Order. You father was part of the Church, and when persecution started he fled west rescuing whatever holy artefacts he could save. Among them were the belongings of a monk who served in the Order and was betrayed by a man in your father's congregation. When you became a hunter you found those belongings, you and your Cell self taught yourselves Bendictions and used them to protect the small Orthodox community you were a part off. Working prayers made you faithful, and when you heard that the Order was reborn you pledged your loyalty.<br /> <br /> [Picture: A monk with an awesome beard walks towards the viewer. His robes are shredded, leaving his impressively muscular chest bare, though with one hand he holds the remains of his robes against a large bleeding wound. Fearsome ghosts surround him but he pays them no head.<br /> <br /> <b>I shall not allow myself to die.<br /> While my duties remain unfulfilled.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Monasteries</span><br /> <br /> The Gravediggers were reforged during decades of Soviet suppression. With the KGB and KSI and their throats they could not afford the luxuries of internal conflict or theological dispute. This is changing, but the legacy of oppression stands strong. The Order of St. Anthony does not divide itself by ideology, but by duties.<br /> <br /> Each duty is named after a monastery. During the cold war members of the Gravedigger\u2019s would say they studied at certain schools as a code to identify themselves. With the old factions of the Conspiracy thoroughly destroyed, the tendency stuck when the new factions were named.<br /> <br /> The Monastery of Blood are the most resolute of the Order, their mission is to face evil without fear and send it back to whatever hell it came from. Vampires, necromancers, and other monsters that cannot or will not turn from the path of evil are their prey. They are made to confess by any means necessary, then placed six feet under.<br /> Speciality: Crafts (Firestarting)<br /> <br /> The Monastery of Sweat serve as the leaders and organisers of a large but loose network of supporters and sympathisers who in turn run the network of safehouses, secure messages and equipment caches. Members are not expected to face monsters directly, but often go into dangerous and unknown territory to prepare the ground.<br /> Speciality: Survival (Safehouses) or Streetwise (Orthodox Community)<br /> <br /> The Monastery of Tears handle those monsters that can be redeemed and offer help to human victims of monsters. The Monastery somewhat specialises in ghosts. They heal the monster's emotional scars, bring justice to past crimes, and return the monsters to the grace of god.<br /> Speciality: Investigation (Records)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stereotypes</span><br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum: Our so called \u201cBrothers in the Faith\u201d. They do god's work but they're still the same heretics they were in 1053.<br /> <br /> The Brotherhood Prizrakov: Don't be fooled by the articles of incorporation. Our records of these witches stretch back almost to the Apostles themselves, which means they may well be older still. A lot of martyrs were made trying to flush them from those mines.<br /> <br /> KSI-21: Ghosts of the \u0421\u043e\u0446\u0438\u0430\u043b\u0438\u0441\u0442\u0438\u0301\u0447\u0435\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0445 suckling from ghosts of the Wehrmacht. They belong in a grave next to all the other horrors of the past century.<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru: There's a reason we built our new headquarters in Serbia, and that is to stay away from the Aegis Kai Doru. They've been around since before Christ and they've spent that time chasing after every last trinket Satan placed to tempt them. One day they'll destroy themselves through their own sin, until then it\u2019s better that the damned prey upon the damned than upon us.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Status</span><br /> <br /> The Order of St. Anthony is a strict military hierarchy, Status is bestowed as a promotion by one\u2019s superiors based on their assessment of who is fit for the duties of the next rank.<br /> <br /> The hierarchy's reach varies dramatically by region. In areas where the Church enjoys strong public and government support the Order has regular but clandestine meetings between members of the Church. In other areas hunters religiously avoid contact with their Conspiracy for extended periods of time; relying on dead letter drops and international travel to hide their association.<br /> <br /> * Wherever you go the Order's network of safehouses is ready to shelter you. You gain a dot in the Safe Place merit, what's more you can hold this dot in reserve to instantly gain access to a safehouse when you most need it \u2013 the Gravediggers have a lot of sympathisers who will hide a hunter in the attic, no questions asked. At the end of a session you may choose to relinquish your free dot and place it back in reserve.<br /> <br /> *** Your name has travelled far among the Order's network of sympathiesrs. You have 2 dot in Allies applied to Order Supporters. Your supporters are rarely combatants, but excel in providing resources, information and a metaphorical smokescreen.<br /> <br /> ***** You\u2019ve endured more than most men. You\u2019ve fought monsters that defied death, and you\u2019ve outlasted them. If you\u2019re reached this Status then the chances are you\u2019ve endured oppression by the soviet union itself. It takes a lot to kill you, by spending a point of Willpower you may gain Resolve boxes of Temporary Health for a scene.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Endowment: Benediction</span><br /> <br /> The secret rites of Benediction predate the East\u2013West Schism by almost a millennium, and so the Order of St Anthony wields them with the same zeal as it\u2019s Catholic counterpart.<br /> <br /> Though the Conspiracy's histories there has been times when scholars would travel to share rites, trade manuscripts and collaborate on research, there has been times when both Conspiracies locked their secrets away, and even times when both tried to steal research and prevent the \u201cheretics\u201d from \u201cdefiling holy power\u201d. While the fundamental principles of Benediction are identical each Conspiracy has their own list of Rites - which Rites are known by which Conspiracy remains the discretion of the storyteller, though the Order of St Anthony are known to favour defensive Benedictions more than their counterparts.<br /> <br /> Some Benedictions have different effects or situational modifiers for different denominations of Christianity. When translating those rites between the Order and the Shadow Congregation the storyteller should adjust the rites to favour the user's denomination. Alternatively the Storyteller may split Benedictions between those that favour Catholicism, those that favour Eastern Orthodoxy and those that favour the user's denomination based on the saint's history and patronage.<br /> <br /> Merit Icon (O)<br /> <br /> You have performed a great deed in the Order\u2019s name and earned the right to carry an Icon of a saint, one whose patronage and history fits your deed, into battle. An Icon grants a single extra point of Willpower that can only be spent on the Benediction petitioning the appropriate saint. This point of Willpower may be spent as part of the activation cost or for extra dice, but the one Willpower per turn rule remains in full force.<br /> <br /> To refill an Icon the Hunter must spend an hour praying with the icon as a focus, Icons can only be refilled once per day.<br /> <br /> Drawback: When the worthy channel Benedictions through Icons of the saints heavenly power remains within the Icon\u2019s earthly form. These Icons are coveted by Witches, Demons and the Aegis Kai Doru. There's power in an Icon, and more in it\u2019s ritual desecration.<br /> <br /> A Hunter who lets their Icon fall into the wrong hands can expect to lose Status, and the Order will go to great lengths to recover Icons consecrated through battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-08-2015, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T06:14:50-07:00","id":291989,"title":"","content":"This is something I promised a long time ago; converting the Order of St. Anthony to a full Conspiracy so they can stand on their own two feet and look the Catholics in the eye. While every section has been expanded the key part is giving them a pre Stalin history. You'll notice though that it's actually a bit barebones; trying to think of that section was what held this project up for so long and in the end I worked around it.<br /> <br /> The other big expansion is probably the Hunters section - which I used as a way to highlight their Conspiracy qualifications, especially with the Bratva hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T06:15:34-07:00","id":291991,"title":"","content":"What's their relations with the Orthodox Churches not under the Patriarch of Moscov? Relations within Orthodox denominations could be tense, especially those not buying into Third Rome bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T08:14:22-07:00","id":292029,"title":"","content":"Probably better than you're expecting. Nothing helps solve internal tensions like an external enemy and the Soviet Union only fell in 1991 - so the majority of members still have the attitude that you stick together no matter what or the KGB will get you.<br /> <br /> In fact, while Putin's government won't just shoot priests suspected of Order membership in their sleep like the Soviets did, KSI-29* is still hunting them, just with higher standards of proof and a bit more respect for the Geneva Convention. And the Order is right next to Greece, since Benedictions look a lot like Witchcraft so they've got the AKD to worry about as well (I personally believe that the AKD is the most dangerous Conspiracy of all).<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW, it's easy to miss because it's only mentioned in the Stereotypes section but the Order is actually headquartered in Ukraine. They used to be in Russia but when they were rebuilding they put the new headquarters in Ukraine.<br /> <br /> Does that answer your question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> * If you don't use KSI-29 in your WoD; replace them with whatever Conspiracy you say serves the Russian government.<br /> <br /> <br /> [edit]BTW everyone, what Saint would be a good one for a Benediction that lets you punch psychics in twilight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-25-2014, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T09:16:17-07:00","id":292087,"title":"","content":"Note that Putin and the Russian Orthodox Church are now allies. See how they quickly denounced Pussy Riot. I don't see Putin attacking organisation related to one of churches that support his rule. Also once Krushchev ascended persecution of Orthodox Church in USSR largely diminished in intensity.<br /> <br /> And also there are strong Orthodox communities outside Soviet Union. Bulgaria, Serbia, Macedonia, Greece and Orthodox minorities in many other countries. Either the organisation is limited to former Soviet Union or relations with other Orthodox communities should be be covered. <br /> <br /> Probably due to isolation Ethiopia has its own organisation. A Compact guarding the Ark of Covenant? Possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T10:03:16-07:00","id":292159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292087#post292087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that Putin and the Russian Orthodox Church are now allies. See how they quickly denounced Pussy Riot. I don't see Putin attacking organisation related to one of churches that support his rule. Also once Krushchev ascended persecution of Orthodox Church in USSR largely diminished in intensity.</div> </div> </div> </div> A difference between the World of Darkness and the real world.<br /> <br /> In the real world the Soviet Union stopped attacking the Church in 1941.<br /> <br /> In the backstory of the Order of St. Anthony the Soviet Union made peace with the Church in 1941 but continued to hunt the Gravediggers until 1991. Putin himself was in the KGB from 1985 to 1990. Even if he wasn't personally involved in hunting Gravediggers, his past will be a contentious issue. Somehow I don't think Putin will like the idea of a large armed, organised, group who dislike him personally.<br /> <br /> So I imagine a lot of smiles in public, and a lot of realpolitik in private.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292087#post292087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also there are strong Orthodox communities outside Soviet Union. Bulgaria, Serbia, Macedonia, Greece and Orthodox minorities in many other countries. Either the organisation is limited to former Soviet Union or relations with other Orthodox communities should be be covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bulgaria, Greece, and Macedonia would probably have minimal presence due to the massive AKD powerbase in the region. I added in a hunter from Serbia to show a bit of that angle and I also moved their headquarters there.<br /> <br /> The angle I'm going for is that refugees arriving in Serbia helped forge stronger ties; they fought monsters together and became friends. I tend to be a theme-first kind of writer, the theme here is that oppression brought them together, so I'll play a little loose with history to promote that theme.<br /> <br /> As for the minority Orthodox communities. Generally speaking, if they sign up and be loyal members of the Gravedigger's organisation they get backup and training in Benedictions. If they don't they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-25-2014, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T12:32:28-07:00","id":292315,"title":"","content":"Serbians and Russians are generally fond of each other, so it's not unreasonable for presence of Gravediggers to be strong there.<br /> <br /> And some minority Orthodox communities may as well sign up with Malleus especially if they are Greek Catholics. There is no more much of resentiment between Orthodox people and Catholics in some countries. I could imagine fierce competition.<br /> <br /> One of major plot hooks could be someone trying to instigate reconciliation between Malleus and Gravediggers because doctrines of Orthodox and Catholic churches are not really that faraway as between let's say, Protestants (except High Church Anglicans) and Catholics. For example maybe Lancea Sanctum grows fast in strength across Europe and it's high time to show those extra heretics their place.<br /> <br /> Also, what's their attitudesto in general to people sifting through pre-Christian folk wisdom to deal with monsters? I feel my group could as well claim influence in Eastern European, so friction is inevitable even if they mainly deal with Hedge denizens and Gentry incursions (and fraternize with some freeholds like a &quot;cancer&quot; conspiracy). Though, they are not fond of Aegis Kai Doru, so desperate alliances might happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T14:23:36-07:00","id":292395,"title":"","content":"The history of their suppression overwrites the reality that the Orthodox church was a key component of the Tsarist Autocracy and the subsequent White armies. They may have heroically resisted but they're still by implication on the side of the proto-fascist anti-Semites. To compare, the MM explicitly incorporates some of the nastier elements of real life Catholicism.<br /> <br /> I know you like going for a more neutral take on conspiracies; that they don't have to have some terrible dark secret, but it rings a little wrong for me here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T14:51:57-07:00","id":292410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292315#post292315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And some minority Orthodox communities may as well sign up with Malleus especially if they are Greek Catholics. There is no more much of resentiment between Orthodox people and Catholics in some countries. I could imagine fierce competition.</div> </div> </div> </div> They may well indeed - though I think that's something for individual storytellers to think about rather than the main write up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292315#post292315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of major plot hooks could be someone trying to instigate reconciliation between Malleus and Gravediggers because doctrines of Orthodox and Catholic churches are not really that faraway as between let's say, Protestants (except High Church Anglicans) and Catholics.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just re-read the Stereotypes section for both the MM and the Long Night and I think that I made them a little too hostile. I'm going to tweak it a tiny bit to match the &quot;respect the hunting, not the religion&quot; angle the MM and the Long Night have for each other.<br /> <br /> While it definately varies at different points in history - I think that most of the time their hostility is inversely proportional to the proximity of the nearest monster. Put a hunter from the MM and the Order in the same room and they'd be screaming &quot;heratic&quot; and might try to kill each other. Put those same two hunters and a vampire in the room and either hunter would gladly sacrafice themselves if it helped the other hunter stake the vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292315#post292315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what's their attitudesto in general to people sifting through pre-Christian folk wisdom to deal with monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on a simple question - does this folk wisdom look like witchcraft? Or to put it another way, does it give you supernatural powers or is it just a monster's weakness?<br /> <br /> If folk-wisdom is just a monster's weakness they'd approve. If it gives you supernatural powers they'd think that &quot;wisdom&quot; is a trap created by Satan to tempt people into Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292395#post292395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The history of their suppression overwrites the reality that the Orthodox church was a key component of the Tsarist Autocracy and the subsequent White armies.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure what you mean here. By &quot;overwrites&quot; do you mean my write-up changes history? I didn't intend to change the reasons for the USSR's persecution of religion, just add that they made the militant wing a primary target.<br /> <br /> Are you objecting to the word &quot;heroically&quot;? I used that word to imply courage rather than morality and don't object to changeing it. Or is it just a more general point that they had a bad history you think needs to be portrayed more?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292395#post292395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To compare, the MM explicitly incorporates some of the nastier elements of real life Catholicism.</div> </div> </div> </div> Look at The Monastery of Blood - it outright says they do the same torture unto confession then kill shtick that the MM do.<br /> <br /> My style is to focus on the things that are unique to the WoD; but it's safe to assume that any real life horrors are unchanged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292395#post292395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you like going for a more neutral take on conspiracies</div> </div> </div> </div> It would be more accurate to say that I have a wider range of moralities in my conspiracies than the official set. The Lord Stewards are outright decent in my opinon, but MI18 are really not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-25-2014, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T14:56:58-07:00","id":292436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The history of their suppression overwrites the reality that the Orthodox church was a key component of the Tsarist Autocracy and the subsequent White armies. They may have heroically resisted but they're still by implication on the side of the proto-fascist anti-Semites. To compare, the MM explicitly incorporates some of the nastier elements of real life Catholicism. </div> </div> </div>Well, and they now support autocracy of Putin. He maybe former member of KGB, but his style is closer to Tsarism.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T15:54:46-07:00","id":292479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does? I don't think I said anything that affects that piece of history in either direction. </div> </div> </div>I think it's more that it isn't really mentioned. I guess that's really more to do with the history being quite minimalistic. They're nobly created to fight monsters, then they're being victims of the Bolsheviks, there's no mention of anything in between. That said, I'm not sure how you'd change that without some lengthy insertion that'd probably just be unnecessary padding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you mean the word &quot;heroic&quot; implies they were morally pure? </div> </div> </div>It does give that impression a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Order; look at The Monastery of Blood - it outright says they do the same torture unto confession then kill shtick that the MM do. </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more of the sidebar on misogyny in the MM. The contrast between the hunters as the moral crusaders of the vigil and the human reality that they might be supporting quite nasty ideologies/political structures at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T16:37:27-07:00","id":292504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292479#post292479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're nobly created to fight monsters</div> </div> </div> </div> One thing I will say is that I do genuinely think that Padre Ambrogino Baudolino had completely noble intentions in founding the MM; and I wanted to match that with Ivanovich Vasin.<br /> <br /> There's a conversation between Baudolino and Lady Lucifuge about Elizabeth B\u00e1thory in either Night Stalkers or Witch Finders (I forgot). You could use that to get a good feeling on what Ivanovich is like in person.<br /> <br /> (Also, while he dosn't have a speaking role it's mentioned elsewhere that there's a third party who participates in those conversations. I suspect that third guy is supposed to have ties to the Canites, but I'm still going to say it's Ivanovich)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292479#post292479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm not sure how you'd change that without some lengthy insertion that'd probably just be unnecessary padding.</div> </div> </div> </div> Me neither, which is why it's not there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292479#post292479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does give that impression a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div> In that case I'll change it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292479#post292479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more of the sidebar on misogyny in the MM. The contrast between the hunters as the moral crusaders of the vigil and the human reality that they might be supporting quite nasty ideologies/political structures at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be honest. I think that torture &amp; murder is a far far far far far worse crime than supporting nasty ideologies or political structures. So I think that moral contrast is covered already.<br /> <br /> Plus, do you really need me to tell you that they support various ideologies and political structures? I think that I made it clear that I'm not trying to morally whitewash (pun not intended) them buy including the torture and murder; shouldn't that and the World of Darkness' default stance of like reality unless stated otherwise be enough to make it completely clear that any real life issues like the White's anti-Semitism also apply/applied to the Order?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:28:22-07:00","id":293079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony#post291969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After those three decades things became easier. When the Great Patriotic War began Stalin and the Eastern Orthodox Church signed a <u>truth</u>, and the Church was allowed to rebuild. The terms of this <u>truth</u> strictly forbade the church from running it\u2019s own military, but those terms were ignored. With support from the Church the Order began to secretly rebuild throughout the Soviet Union and even beyond, far from the eyes of anyone searching for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should be &quot;truce&quot;, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/291969-conspiracy-the-order-of-st-anthony?p=292029#post292029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW everyone, what Saint would be a good one for a Benediction that lets you punch psychics in twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I'm reminded of the tale of<b> St. Peter</b> knocking Simon Magus out of the air, but that isn't really the same as being in twilight ...<br /> <br /> <b>St. Michael</b> (the Archangel) would make sense for letting you engage ephemeral entities in combat. Probably your best bet. That doesn't really fit with <i>psychics</i> specifically, though, if that's what you have in mind.<br /> <br /> OrthodoxWiki gives us <b><a href=\"http://orthodoxwiki.org/Patron_saint#Against_demons_and_witchcraft\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> patron saints</b> &quot;against demons and witchcraft&quot;, but I'm not really sure why - it doesn't give reasons they're associated with it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.oodegr.com/english/anatolikes/astral_projection.htm\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> thoroughly reputable-looking site assures that <b>St. Paul</b> could astral-project: &quot;For I, albeit absent in body but present in spirit...&quot; That would allow you to punch psychics, presumably, but it's more emphasizing <i>observation</i>. Similarly, <a href=\"http://www.williamjames.com/Folklore/ASTRAL.htm\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> site suggests<b> St. Augustine</b> could do it, but ... yeah, I'm scraping the bottom of the barrel at this point. Ah, <b>Padre Pio</b> has a lot of references to &quot;bilocation&quot; surrounding him as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:47:43-07:00","id":293105,"title":"","content":"I did specifically have psychics in mind. KSI-29 is a sadly unfinished Conspiracy by Glamourweaver which can be described as Orpheus meats the KGB. When I say the Order has an issue with ex-Soviet hunters; I personally think KSI-29, so a Benediction that lets them fight psychics in Twilight is a must. Sadly St. Michael is taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T16:42:57-07:00","id":293297,"title":"","content":"It's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/36179-ksi-21-the-committee-for-special-research-section-21-starting-now-more-to-come\">KSI-2<b>1</b></a>.<br /> <br /> In case anyone else tries to look it up.<br /> <br /> How about St. Jerome, patron saint of Librarians? He was a staunch theological debater (and, coincidentally, my patron saint). Feast day's September 30th.<br /> <br /> St. Dymphna, patron saint of Troubled Minds? May 15.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:58:48-07:00","id":293905,"title":"","content":"Damn; I'm <b>constantly</b> making that mistake.<br /> <br /> I'm using St Jerome <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/Chapter_Four:_Theology\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>to power a anti-magic Benediction (assume that the Order has a variant that treats Eastern Orthodox as the true faith); St. Dymphna might be a possibility, but it's still a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-27-2014, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:09:00-07:00","id":294068,"title":"","content":"Yeah - we just need to canonize a saint of ESPers, and then you'll be all set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:19:33-07:00","id":294075,"title":"","content":"Funny thing, I stumbled on that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://weeklyworldnews.com/headlines/10299/3-out-of-10-saints-were-psychic/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i2.wp.com/weeklyworldnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/07/psychic_saints.jpg?fit=375%2C200\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://weeklyworldnews.com/headlines/10299/3-out-of-10-saints-were-psychic/\" target=\"_blank\"> 3 OUT OF 10 SAINTS WERE PSYCHIC </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://weeklyworldnews.com/headlines/10299/3-out-of-10-saints-were-psychic/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://weeklyworldnews.com/headlines/10299/3-out-of-10-saints-were-psychic/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Nearly 30% of all Catholic saints actually possessed some paranormal powers or had psychic experiences! </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Probably Daniel Stylite qualifies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:45:33-07:00","id":294163,"title":"","content":"I saw that headline while looking myself; but I didn't think that title could possibly contain any genuine theology. I guess I'll give it a read after all.<br /> <br /> I'm currently considering Saint Joshua (from Exodus) as the Patron Saint of Spies. It's not like I have anything better. Edit: another idea - Raymond Nonnatus, the patron saint of keeping secrets to defend against spies. I wonder if I can work in that lock ritual somehow. Sadly I can't find anything suggesting he's honoured in Eastern Orthodox Christianity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-27-2014, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T15:01:50-07:00","id":294179,"title":"","content":"Maybe you could go with <a href=\"http://www.catholic.org/saints/saint.php?saint_id=1154\" target=\"_blank\">Saint Agabus</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T15:11:38-07:00","id":294184,"title":"","content":"You know, it's handy that IRL there is basically a Saint for everything, because we will probably never exhaust Benedictions ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T16:28:49-07:00","id":294264,"title":"","content":"We haven't even finished with the obvious Saints yet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I mean, how come Joan of Arc is missing? Joan of Arc! (I know I homebrewed one for her see post #16, but still... they left out Joan of Arc!)<br /> <br /> Anyway, I almost ended up using St Nicholas as the Patron of the falsely accused but I just couldn't resist creating a Benediction that petitions Santa Claus instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Gifts of St. Nicholas<br /> <br /> Though the Order claims St. Anthony as it's patron, the Gravediggers honour St. Nicholas as the saint who actually protected them during their darkest days. As the patron of the falsely accused and the secret provider of charity it was St. Nicholas who provided for the Gravediggers when they were at their lowest. The Gifts may only be invoked once per Session.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower Point<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Benediction<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The hunters meet someone who has even greater needs than them. Christian morals obligate them to help, at the very least refusal inflicts the Guilty condition.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The hunters meet someone who is willing to help them, discretely. Take half Benediction (rounding up) dots in Allies, Contacts, Resources or Safe Place. Alternatively you get a one time free transport. Dots fade at the end of the session.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Take an additional dot.<br /> <b>Suggested Modifiers: </b>In a predomimently Christian area (+2), of the same Denomination as the hunters (+1), in a predominately secular area (-2), in the middle of the wilderness (-5), invoked on 6th December the feast day of St Nicholas (+5).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> At the risk of getting back into the history debate; what I mean by using the protector of the falsely accused is that he Soviets denied the existence of the Order and used various trumped up charges instead. As for the secular thing; secular people aren't less likely to be virtuous, but the idea is that it's harder for Saints to work through them.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Something of St. Something <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower Point<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Composure + Benediction<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> I'll think of something.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens.<br /> <b>Success:</b> For the remainder of the scene the Hunter may perceive astrally projecting psychics and witches in Twilight. In addition the hunter may physically interact with them, usually violently. If the Hunter is in physical contact with a Blessed Item (such as those created by the Sanctification of the Blessed Virgin) then that item may also physically interact with projecting psychics. This dosn't harm the psychic if he's already half-way though the Blessed Item.<br /> <br /> The Something of St. Something does not provide any defence against psychic powers used to hide. The True Sight of St. Abel is required for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Hunter gains protection from tricks psychics might use to remain invisible. This works as though a single success in the True Sight of St. Abel had been invested in the hunter - but only for the purpose of seeing through psychic illusions. This benefit does not stack with an actual Invocation of the True Sight.<br /> <b>Suggested Modifiers: </b>The Hunter stands on consecrated ground (+2), The hunter smeers fresh grapes on his eyes (+1), Invoked on September 1'st, feast day of St Joshua (+5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-27-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T17:52:12-07:00","id":294326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We haven't even finished with the obvious Saints yet I mean, how come Joan of Arc is missing? Joan of Arc! (I know I homebrewed one for her see post #16, but still... they left out Joan of Arc!) </div> </div> </div>Alright, Jeanne's Benediction was done nicely.<br /> <br /> General question, do you also homebrew Benedictions for Old Testament figures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T19:07:33-07:00","id":294411,"title":"","content":"St John.<br /> <br /> St. John's Wort, specifically.<br /> <br /> Under some folklore, burning it lets you see fairies.<br /> <br /> Just thought of that - sadly, Wort of St. John sounds kinda eh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edit